[{"category":"section","location":"#ExampleMessagePassingRules","page":"Overview","text":"The ExampleNormal node is a normal distribution with a known variance, with its belief propagation and variational rules and its average energy. It is the node of MessagePassingRulesBase's tutorial Your first node, packaged.\n\ntip: Replace this page\nThis page follows the layout every node page of a rule package follows: overview, definition, interfaces, algorithm, supported rules, example, limitations and API. Keep the sections and replace their content with your node's.\n\ninfo: Where these rules run\nThe ReactiveMP engine runs these rules on a factor graph, which RxInfer builds from a model. The examples here call the rules directly.","title":"ExampleMessagePassingRules"},{"category":"section","location":"#Overview","page":"Overview","text":"Use the node for an observation or a latent variable with a normal distribution whose variance is known. Its mean can be another variable of the model, observed or not.","title":"Overview"},{"category":"section","location":"#Definition","page":"Overview","text":"f(mathrmout mu v) = mathcalN(mathrmout mid mu v)","title":"Definition"},{"category":"section","location":"#Interfaces","page":"Overview","text":"using ExampleMessagePassingRules, MessagePassingRulesBase, ExponentialFamily, BayesBase\nMessagePassingRulesBase.nodespec(ExampleNormal)\nNodeSpec: ExampleNormal (stochastic)\n  interfaces:        out, μ (aliases: mean), v\n  default algorithm: MessagePassingRulesBase.DefaultAlgorithm()\n  static inputs:     none\n  defined:           src/ExampleMessagePassingRules.jl:60\n\nname aliases meaning messages and marginals its rules take\nout none the variable the distribution is over normal or observed messages, any marginal\nμ mean the mean normal or observed messages, any marginal\nv none the variance, positive a PointMass","title":"Interfaces"},{"category":"section","location":"#Algorithm","page":"Overview","text":"The node uses DefaultAlgorithm, which has no parameters, so a model names none. It declares no dependencies of its own: its rules take what the default scheme delivers.","title":"Algorithm"},{"category":"section","location":"#Supported-rules","page":"Overview","text":"MessagePassingRulesBase.rule_coverage(ExampleNormal)\nRule coverage for ExampleNormal\n                 │ DefaultAlgorithm\n  → out          │ ✓×2             \n  → μ            │ ✓×2             \n  → v            │                 \n  average energy │ ✓               \n\nBelief propagation, towards out from the messages on μ and v, and towards μ from the messages on out and v: the variances add. The log scale is 0.\nVariational message passing, towards out from the marginals q(μ) and q(v), and towards μ from q(out) and q(v): only the mean of the other marginal counts.\nThe average energy, from q(out), q(μ) and q(v).","title":"Supported rules"},{"category":"section","location":"#Example","page":"Overview","text":"The message towards out from a normal message on the mean:\n\n@call_message_update_rule(\n    node = ExampleNormal, target = :out,\n    m = (μ = NormalMeanVariance(1.0, 2.0), v = PointMass(0.5)),\n)\n\u001b[0m\u001b[1mRuleResult\u001b[22m  message of ExampleNormal towards :out  \u001b[90m· belief propagation\u001b[39m\n  \u001b[0m\u001b[1mExampleNormal\u001b[22m\n    out  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m◀══  target\u001b[22m\u001b[39m  \u001b[32mExponentialFamily.NormalMeanVariance{Float64}(μ=1.0, v=2.5)\u001b[39m\n    μ    \u001b[36m──▶  m\u001b[39m  ExponentialFamily.NormalMeanVariance{Float64}(μ=1.0, v=2.0)\n    v    \u001b[36m──▶  m\u001b[39m  PointMass{Float64}(0.5)\n  result     ExponentialFamily.NormalMeanVariance{Float64}(μ=1.0, v=2.5)\n  logscale   \u001b[0m0  (declared)\n  algorithm  DefaultAlgorithm()\n  rule       m[:μ]::Union{BayesBase.PointMass, ExponentialFamily.UnivariateNormalDistributionsFamily, ExponentialFamily.UnivariateGaussianDistributionsFamily}, m[:v]::BayesBase.PointMass  @ src/ExampleMessagePassingRules.jl:73\n\u001b[90m  and 1 other rule for this target\u001b[39m\n\nThe variance of the message on μ, 2, and the variance of the node, 0.5, add to 2.5. A variance that is not positive raises a RuleInputError:\n\ntry\n    @call_message_update_rule(node = ExampleNormal, target = :out, m = (μ = PointMass(1.0), v = PointMass(-1.0)))\ncatch err\n    print(first(split(sprint(showerror, err), \"\\n  rule at\")))\nend\nRuleInputError: the message rule for ExampleNormal towards :out under MessagePassingRulesBase.DefaultAlgorithm refuses its inputs: the variance `v` must be positive; got -1.0\n  inputs: m[:v]::BayesBase.PointMass{Float64}, m[:μ]::BayesBase.PointMass{Float64}","title":"Example"},{"category":"section","location":"#Limitations","page":"Overview","text":"The variance must be a PointMass: there are no rules for a random variance.\nUnivariate only.\nThe variational rules declare no log scale.","title":"Limitations"},{"category":"section","location":"#API","page":"Overview","text":"","title":"API"},{"category":"module","location":"#ExampleMessagePassingRules","page":"Overview","text":"ExampleMessagePassingRules\n\nThe ExampleNormal node and its rules: a normal distribution with a known variance, the node of MessagePassingRulesBase's tutorial Your first node, packaged.\n\nReplace it with your own nodes: declare each with @define_factor_node, define its rules with @define_message_update_rule, @define_marginal_update_rule and @define_average_energy, and test every rule in test/.\n\nExamples\n\njulia> using MessagePassingRulesBase, ExponentialFamily, BayesBase\n\njulia> result = @call_message_update_rule(\n           node = ExampleNormal, target = :out,\n           m = (μ = NormalMeanVariance(1.0, 2.0), v = PointMass(0.5)),\n       );\n\njulia> getresult(result) ≈ NormalMeanVariance(1.0, 2.5)\ntrue\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ExampleMessagePassingRules"},{"category":"type","location":"#ExampleMessagePassingRules.ExampleNormal","page":"Overview","text":"ExampleNormal(μ, v)\n\nA normal distribution over out with mean μ and variance v, as a stochastic factor node: f(out, μ, v) = N(out | μ, v). Called with its parameters, it is that distribution, a NormalMeanVariance.\n\nInterfaces\n\nout: the variable the distribution is over.\nμ: the mean, also named mean.\nv: the variance, a PointMass.\n\nRules\n\nbelief propagation, towards out from m(μ) and m(v), and towards μ from m(out) and m(v): the variances add, with log scale 0;\nvariational message passing, towards out from q(μ) and q(v), and towards μ from q(out) and q(v);\nthe average energy, from q(out), q(μ) and q(v).\n\nThe variance must be positive; every rule checks it.\n\nSee also ExampleMessagePassingRules.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ExampleMessagePassingRules.ExampleNormal"}]
